###### **NOMENCLATURE** 

A – specific mass transfer area, 1/m; 

_d_ – drop diameter, m; 

_d_ 32 – average (Sauter) drop diameter, m; 

_Dimpeller_ – impeller diameter, m; 

_Dtank_ – tank diameter, m; 

_Dm_ – molecular diffusivity, m<sup>2</sup> /s; 

_Dm,cont_ , _Dm,disp_ – molecular diffusivities of continuous and disperse phases correspondingly, m<sup>2</sup> /s; _g_ – gravity acceleration, m/s<sup>2</sup> ; 

_k_ – mass transfer coefficient, m/s; 

_kcont_ , _kdisp_ – mass transfer coefficients, from the side of continuous and disperse phases correspondingly m/s; 

_kvol_ – volumetric mass transfer coefficients, 1/s; 

_te_ – a surface renewal time 

_T_ – residence time, s; 

_vt,baffles_ – tangential velocity near the baffle; m/s; 

_Wbaffles_ – baffle width, m; 

_μcont_ , _μdisp_ – dynamic viscosities of continuous and disperse phases correspondingly, Pa<sup>.</sup> s; 

_ρcont_ , _ρdisp_ – dencities of continuous and disperse phases correspondingly, kg/m<sup>3</sup> ; 

_εavg_ – average energy dissipation rate, w/kg; 

_εmax_ – maximum energy dissipation rate, w/kg; 

_φ_ – volume concentration of disperse phase.
